From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: disable harfbuzz utilities (Apple meson cross file lacks objcpp)

3.0.24's bumped HarfBuzz util/ requires an 'objcpp' binary in the meson cross
file on Darwin, which VLC's generated cross file does not define, failing the
Apple contrib build (harfbuzz/util/meson.build: 'objcpp' compiler binary not
defined in cross file [binaries] section). The utilities are CLI tools libvlc
never links; disable them so only the library (incl. coretext shaping) builds.
This mirrors the VLC 4 patch of the same name.
---
--- a/contrib/src/harfbuzz/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/harfbuzz/rules.mak
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ HARFBUZZ_CONF := -Dfreetype=enabled \
 	-Dgobject=disabled \
 	-Ddocs=disabled \
 	-Dtests=disabled \
-	-Dgpu_demo=disabled
+	-Dgpu_demo=disabled \
+	-Dutilities=disabled
 
 ifdef HAVE_DARWIN_OS
 HARFBUZZ_CONF += -Dcoretext=enabled
